4|0@gtaonline^1439870654#cu6pe4v:Psychko$:In armed helicopters? Absolutely people grief in those. Unarmed helicopters? In my experience being griefed by someone in a civilian chopper is extremely rare. That doesn't change my assertion that by the time a helicopter is within Launcher range, you can easily identify whether or not it's armed and act accordingly, there is no need to have a "shoot first and ask questions later" mentality. If anything, that's one way to guarantee conflict. If you shoot me down while I'm flying around harmlessly, then you guarantee I'll be coming after you and will repay the favour many times over. When a helicopter approaches my position, I'll take precautions and wait until I can identify what I'm dealing with. If it's an armed helicopter, I know I need to remain vigilant in case they are hostile and can take appropriate action. If it's a civilian helicopter, quite often it's simply a player travelling from A to B. If that player decides to land, I'll again be prepared in case they get out of the helicopter and start shooting, but I won't fire upon someone simply because they're in the air and within Launcher range. edit: grammar
