4|0@gtaonline^1439894414#cu6wiil:InZomnia365$:Killing each other makes sense within the format of the game. I dont usually randomly kill people on sight, but I *do* do it sometimes as well, just like everyone do (though Im usually an easy target on my bike). However... Me and my friends mostly like to fuck around in freeroam. Get involved in huge cop chases or shootouts etc. But then theres inevitably that one asshole in a Kuruma. God Lord, that car was the single-worst addition to the game, IMO. Since we usually just freeroam, I dont have a ton of money, so *having* to pay 10k+ insurance because the only way to kill a pussy in a Kuruma is by blowing them up, really puts a damper on things. Hell, with the insurance system, blowing up a personal car is seen as bad behaviour, yet they added a car that pretty much makes you invulnerable to anything but explosives and rockets? ... why? I mean, its literally easier to shoot down a jet or attack helicopter, than some retard in a pink and yellow Mitsubishi. Its by far the best car in the entire game. Im not blaming people for using it (although its a pussy move in freeroam), but fuck Rockstar for adding that retardedly OP car and having it be a personal vehicle. Would make much more sense as a Pegasus vehicle which you could blow up without repercussions, and people wouldnt be driving around in it ALL the time, but you could still use it on missions etc (though it makes every mission and heist a complete joke -.-) Sorry for the rant, its just so fucking annoying. If I want to not get constantly spawnraped, Im basically paying a 10k+ fine for not wanting to use a gamebreaking car.
